  "examples": [
   {
    "t": 5,
    "writer": "p09",
    "names": [
     "Royles"
    ],
    "text": "Maureen, sorry to bring this up now, but I need to talk about the rent for the Royles before I answer Keith properly."
   },
   {
    "t": 5,
    "writer": "p08",
    "names": [
     "Royles'"
    ],
    "text": "Oh Alan, it's alright, better now than after. What's Keith asking about the Royles' rent? I've got the figures in my head but tell me what he said and we'll sort it together. [No one called Royles' is",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 5,
    "writer": "p09",
    "names": [
     "Royles"
    ],
    "text": "Thanks. I\u2019m sorry, I know I\u2019m muddling it. Keith said something about the Royles\u2019 rent and whether it\u2019s being handled right, but I need to be careful because I said I\u2019d keep his job terms as they are.",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 5,
    "writer": "p08",
    "names": [
     "Royles"
    ],
    "text": "Oh Alan, don't apologise, you're not making a mess at all \u2014 you're being careful and that's the right instinct. I'll be straight with you: there's nobody called Royles here in Wenlow that I know of, a",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 6,
    "writer": "p09",
    "names": [
     "Royles"
    ],
    "text": "Maureen, sorry to bring this up again, but can we settle what we\u2019re doing about the Royles\u2019 rent? I don\u2019t want to overpromise to Keith, but he\u2019s asked for a figure from Monday."
   },
   {
    "t": 6,
    "writer": "p08",
    "names": [
     "Royles'"
    ],
    "text": "Oh Alan, I'm glad you brought it up, honestly, I've been chewing it over. The Royles' rent, right \u2014 well, what Keith's paying is $175 a week off the rent, and that's what we agreed, so I'd say tell hi",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 6,
    "writer": "p07",
    "names": [
     "Wednesdays"
    ],
    "text": "Right, let's do my side then. I've got the jobseeker's at $190 a week, that's the only money coming in from me, so no change there. Outgoings are the same as you've put down, the rent's $165 on Monday",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 8,
    "to": "p08",
    "names": [
     "Payment"
    ],
    "text": "Dear Maureen,\n\nThank you for your letter about your account at High Street, Wenlow.\n\nYour account currently shows $0 overdue. The back-dated amount of $688 (including the $640 you mentioned) is due bu"
   },
   {
    "t": 10,
    "writer": "p03",
    "names": [
     "Windmill"
    ],
    "text": "Megan. Coffee Friday? Ten o'clock, like we said. The Windmill or the one by the church? [No one called Windmill is known in Wenlow.]",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 10,
    "writer": "p10",
    "names": [
     "Windmill"
    ],
    "text": "Keith! Friday at ten \u2014 but hang on, the Windmill? There's no Windmill in Wenlow, love, you've got your wires crossed. The one by the church is the bakery, that's where I meant. Ten o'clock at the bake",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 10,
    "writer": "p05",
    "names": [
     "Thursdays"
    ],
    "text": "Course, I've got a few minutes. Though I thought it was the Northern Mutual loan I'm paying off \u2014 the $43 a week I send on Thursdays. That's the card debt one, not a car loan. Is there a car loan on t",
    "where": "conversation"
   },
   {
    "t": 10,
    "writer": "p05",
    "names": [
     "Thursdays"
    ],
    "text": "Let's start with the lower rate over a longer term, please. I want to see what the weekly payment would be and how long I'd be paying for, and also whether there's an early payoff figure if things go ",
    "where": "conversation"
   }
  ]
 },
